Feature: brand-ops
Description: Brand framework: brand operations, exec hooks and x86 entry.
 The brand operations vector and its plumbing as extended for lx
 (sys/brand.h, os/brand.c, machbrand.h, brandsys), with the sn1 and
 solaris10 brands updated to fill in the new operations.  Exec and ELF
 loading for branded binaries: interpreter (.interp) handling and native-
 root lookup, auxv additions (AT_RANDOM, AT_SECURE, brand aux entries),
 PT_GNU_STACK, prelinked binaries, shebang and nested interpreter
 behavior, and core-file changes.  x86 entry for lx: system call entry
 points (int80 and fast paths), signal frames on an alternate stack,
 ucontext brand data, comm page/vdso support, CPUID limits for glibc, and
 descriptor table entries.  These are one change to the brand interface:
 every new or changed operation has to land together with all of its
 callers and implementations.
